# Deploy (GitHub Pages)

Live URL: https://namenameemail.github.io/rasterscape/

Static site lives in sibling repo:

`/home/name/Desktop/web/namenameemail.github.io/rasterscape/`

Source stays here (`rasterscape`). Pages repo only gets the built files.

## How

```sh
npm run deploy
```

Script: [`scripts/deploy.sh`](scripts/deploy.sh).

1. `vite build` with `base: './'` (subdir-safe asset paths; skips `tsc` — full `npm run build` often fails on existing type debt).
2. Replace `../namenameemail.github.io/rasterscape/` with `dist/`.
3. Commit + push that repo (`origin`, current branch).

Override pages path: `PAGES_DIR=/other/path npm run deploy`.

## Rules

- Do not put source into the pages repo — only `dist` contents.
- Do not change `base` back to `/` without updating deploy; absolute `/assets/…` breaks under `/rasterscape/`.
- After deploy, wait a minute for Pages; hard-refresh if an old bundle is cached.
